Architectural choices:
  - Dropped the prisma DI param. The Track 1 pattern (and reading-advantage
    migration) imports db directly. DI would require a parallel Drizzle DI
    pattern that doesn't exist yet, and the only caller (route.ts:210) is in
    Phase 2 scope anyway \u2014 changing it now is cheaper than maintaining
    backwards-compat.
  - Nested includes \u2192 fanned-out queries. Prisma's 'include' was emitting
    JOINs against the curriculum graph (unit \u2192 lessons \u2192 standards +
    lessonCompletions). Drizzle equivalents:
      \u00b7 1 unit-batch SELECT
      \u00b7 N per-unit lesson SELECTs (one per unit; bounded by unit count)
      \u00b7 N per-unit lesson_standards SELECTs (batched by lessonIds IN array)
      \u00b7 N per-unit lesson_completions SELECTs (batched by lessonIds + studentId)
    The fan-out is O(units) regardless of lesson count, which mirrors the
    original Prisma round-trip count and avoids a 4-way JOIN with multiple
    1:N relations (which would multiplicatively explode row counts).
  - LessonCompletionStatus inlined as a local type rather than added to
    lib/enums.ts \u2014 only one file uses it. Promote to enums.ts when a second
    consumer needs it.

